<title>USA: U.S. Medical Instruments IPO delayed.</title>
<headline>U.S. Medical Instruments IPO delayed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The initial public offering of U.S. Medical Products Inc, which was scheduled for November, has been postponed until December or January, according to the lead underwriter for the deal, Rodman &amp; Renshaw Inc.</p>
<p>Terms and price range for the issue have not been disclosed.</p>
<p>The company designs and makes disposable medical products to protect health-care workers from spread of infectious diseases.</p>
</text>
